{
  "scenario": "A fictional residential tenancy, read through LKIF Core's legal and commonsense layers. A member of a legislative body introduces a bill, and the body enacts a statute bearing three norms: an obligation on landlords to keep a dwelling in repair, a permission for tenants to withhold rent once they have given notice of disrepair, and a prohibition on evicting without a court order; the behaviours the norms qualify are compared as obliged, allowed and disallowed. A landlord and a tenant play their roles in the context of a lease, which bears the tenant's obligation to pay rent and which the tenant promised; the tenant's written notice, borne by a letter, leads to the landlord's repairs. Each action has its actor, requirement, result and the moment it took up, and the moments are ordered in time.",
